#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "376b8af6-29bc-55ae-be7a-9659c2559891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303289} {:answer/id #uuid "38f1d0b5-d56f-5080-be06-dd709d489c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38f1d0b5-d56f-5080-be06-dd709d489c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303290} :answer-field/id #uuid "1965bafe-8660-507f-9547-8ea44caad029" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303288}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9258d52-01b3-55d0-afcb-ea66a3cfa2e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-316584" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14062337/assets/f38424364e3d4efd8ebc416974163e3eb87b3350c0c6b8ec7f5ae4ea69339824.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,4\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
